{
	"id": "lpc32",
	"tile": 32,
	"pixels_from": "files",
	"_readme": [
		"Hand-drawn Liberated Pixel Cup terrain, cut cell by cell out of the sheets under",
		"data/imports/tiles/lpc32/. Twelve ids in gb16's order with gb16's solid and decor flags,",
		"which is what lets every shipped map, every fixture and both editor couplings carry on",
		"unchanged: only the pixels moved.",
		"",
		"A tile names its file and a CELL in it, column then row. There is no ramp: the colours",
		"are the artists' and the style does not recolour them - that is the whole difference",
		"between this bank and an authored one.",
		"",
		"Water and path also name a RING: the twelve transition pieces LPC draws around each of",
		"these sheets, and the ground each is an edge against. The generator composes the 47 shapes",
		"a cell can take out of QUARTERS of those pieces and appends them to the atlas; the world",
		"picks one per cell from its eight neighbours. A map still spells one tile id per cell, so",
		"nothing about the map format, the editor round trips or the play sessions changed.",
		"",
		"Water is an edge against grass AND against path, in that order: the village and hollow",
		"ponds sit in grass and the cave's sits in dirt. Path is an edge against grass only - where",
		"a path meets water it is the WATER that draws the boundary, so it is drawn once.",
		"",
		"The files block travels in the pack, which is about two kilobytes of names and URLs. It",
		"is left there rather than filtered out: credits.json is the file a credits screen reads,",
		"and an exclude rule that has to keep growing is worse than the bytes.",
		"",
		"tools/fetch_tiles.sh fetches every file with a `url` into data/imports/tiles/lpc32/.",
		"plants.png has none on purpose: it ships as a zip from its OpenGameArt page, so the one",
		"sheet inside it is extracted and placed by hand, and the script says so rather than failing.",
		"",
		"Every file names the sha256 of its sheet, and fetch_tiles.sh puts nothing in place that",
		"does not match it; test_imported_art holds the committed sheets to the same sums. The urls",
		"read the LPC repository at a COMMIT, whose files were checked against the committed sheets",
		"on 2026-09-13: a branch is whatever the next push makes it, and a commit names the bytes."
	],
